# Riverpod 3.x Codegen — Provider Naming

## How class name → provider variable name

Riverpod codegen strips the `Notifier` suffix from the class name, then lowercases the first letter:

| Class | Generated provider variable |
|---|---|
| `class FeedNotifier` | `feedProvider` |
| `class AuthNotifier` | `authProvider` |
| `class ReportNotifier` | `reportProvider` |
| `class ResolveReportNotifier` | `resolveReportProvider` |
| `class InboxNotifier` | `inboxProvider` |

**NOT** `feedNotifierProvider`, `authNotifierProvider`, etc.

## Accessing notifier methods

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT — call .notifier on the generated variable
ref.read(feedProvider.notifier).refresh();
ref.read(reportProvider.notifier).submit(...);
ref.read(resolveReportProvider(reportId).notifier).resolve(...);

// ❌ WRONG — these don't exist
ref.read(feedNotifierProvider.notifier).refresh();
ref.read(reportNotifierProvider.notifier).submit(...);
```

## Watching state

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT
final feedAsync = ref.watch(feedProvider);
final isLoading = ref.watch(reportProvider).isLoading;

// Parameterized notifier (family)
final resolveState = ref.watch(resolveReportProvider(reportId));
```

## Non-notifier providers (function-based)

Function-based providers use the function name directly:

```dart
@riverpod
FeedItem getFeedItem(Ref ref) => ...
// → getFeedItemProvider

@riverpod
Stream<List<Report>> pendingReports(Ref ref) => ...
// → pendingReportsProvider
```

## Quick check before writing any ref.watch/ref.read

1. Find the class name in `<feature>_providers.dart`
2. Remove `Notifier` suffix → lowercase first letter → append `Provider`
3. If parameterized (`build(String id)`): it becomes a family → call as `xyzProvider(id)`
